|passage=And so it had always '''pleased''' M. Stutz to expect great things from the dark young man whom he had first seen in his early twenties ; and his expectations had waxed rather than waned on hearing the faint bruit of the love of Ivor and Virginia—for Virginia, M. Stutz thought, would bring fineness to a point in a man like Ivor Marlay, […].}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Paint a Vulgar Picture|lyricist=w:Morrissey|composer=w:Johnny Marr|album=w:Strangeways, Here We Come|artist=w:The Smiths|year=1987|passage=World tour, media whore / "'''Please''' the Press in Belgium!" / This was your life}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2024 October 2|author=Philip Haigh|title=Different types of passengers require different types of fare|journal=RAIL|issue=1019|page=54|text=How can an operator be, at the same time, top for overall satisfaction and bottom for value for money? I turned to Anthony Smith for the answer, leaning on his 20 years running Transport Focus and its predecessors.<br>It's commuters, he explained. "You can't '''please''' commuters, you can only not displease them."}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|ergative}} To [[desire]]; to [[will]]; to be pleased by.
